            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-66418",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "urllib3: urllib3: Unbounded decompression chain leads to resource exhaustion"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "urllib3 is a user-friendly HTTP client library for Python. Starting in version 1.24 and prior to 2.6.0, the number of links in the decompression chain was unbounded allowing a malicious server to insert a virtually unlimited number of compression steps leading to high CPU usage and massive memory allocation for the decompressed data. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.6.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-66418",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-66418\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: urllib3\nFixed Version: 2.6.0\nLink: [CVE-2025-66418](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-66418)\nurllib3 is a user-friendly HTTP client library for Python. Starting in version 1.24 and prior to 2.6.0, the number of links in the decompression chain was unbounded allowing a malicious server to insert a virtually unlimited number of compression steps leading to high CPU usage and massive memory allocation for the decompressed data. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.6.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-66418**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|urllib3|2.6.0|[CVE-2025-66418](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-66418)|\n\nurllib3 is a user-friendly HTTP client library for Python. Starting in version 1.24 and prior to 2.6.0, the number of links in the decompression chain was unbounded allowing a malicious server to insert a virtually unlimited number of compression steps leading to high CPU usage and massive memory allocation for the decompressed data. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.6.0."
              },
