            {
              "id": "AWS-0132",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "S3 encryption should use Customer Managed Keys"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Encryption using AWS keys provides protection for your S3 buckets. To gain greater control over encryption, such as key rotation, access policies, and auditability, use customer managed keys (CMKs) with SSE-KMS.\nNote that SSE-KMS is not supported for S3 server access logging destination buckets; in such cases, use SSE-S3 instead.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0132",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration AWS-0132\nType: Terraform Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: S3 encryption should use Customer Managed Keys\nMessage: Bucket does not encrypt data with a customer managed key.\nLink: [AWS-0132](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0132)\nEncryption using AWS keys provides protection for your S3 buckets. To gain greater control over encryption, such as key rotation, access policies, and auditability, use customer managed keys (CMKs) with SSE-KMS.\nNote that SSE-KMS is not supported for S3 server access logging destination buckets; in such cases, use SSE-S3 instead.\n",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration AWS-0132**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Terraform Security Check|HIGH|S3 encryption should use Customer Managed Keys|Bucket does not encrypt data with a customer managed key.|[AWS-0132](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/aws-0132)|\n\nEncryption using AWS keys provides protection for your S3 buckets. To gain greater control over encryption, such as key rotation, access policies, and auditability, use customer managed keys (CMKs) with SSE-KMS.\nNote that SSE-KMS is not supported for S3 server access logging destination buckets; in such cases, use SSE-S3 instead.\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0001",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Can elevate its own privileges"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A program inside the container can elevate its own privileges and run as root, which might give the program control over the container and node."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0001\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nCheck: Can elevate its own privileges\nMessage: Container 'app' of Pod 'demo' should set 'securityContext.allowPrivilegeEscalation' to false\nLink: [KSV-0001](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001)\nA program inside the container can elevate its own privileges and run as root, which might give the program control over the container and node.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0001**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|MEDIUM|Can elevate its own privileges|Container 'app' of Pod 'demo' should set 'securityContext.allowPrivilegeEscalation' to false|[KSV-0001](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001)|\n\nA program inside the container can elevate its own privileges and run as root, which might give the program control over the container and node."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0003",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The container should drop all default capabilities and add only those that are needed for its execution."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0003\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all\nMessage: Container 'app' of Pod 'demo' should add 'ALL' to 'securityContext.capabilities.drop'\nLink: [KSV-0003](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003)\nThe container should drop all default capabilities and add only those that are needed for its execution.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0003**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|LOW|Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all|Container 'app' of Pod 'demo' should add 'ALL' to 'securityContext.capabilities.drop'|[KSV-0003](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003)|\n\nThe container should drop all default capabilities and add only those that are needed for its execution."
              },
              "properties": {
